# Build output
*.exe
*.o

# Windows resource blob. Regenerated from icon/recicon.rc by the Makefile rule, so the
# source of truth (the .rc and the .ico) is versioned and the derived COFF is not.
*.res

# Third party runtime libraries. Not vendored on purpose: SDL3 and SDL3_image are
# versioned upstream, and a repository should not be the place people get their copy
# from. See README.md for where they come from and where they go.
*.dll

# Upstream packages downloaded during setup
*.zip

# Lucida Console ships with Windows and is Bigelow & Holmes property - usable on a
# machine that already has it, never redistributable from a public repository. It is no
# longer asked for: the shipped face is font/DejaVuSansMono.ttf, which is monospaced AND
# redistributable. The rule stays so a stray copy in font/ cannot be committed by
# accident. See CLAUDE.md section 5.
font/lucon.ttf

# Frame captures taken while verifying rendering
shot.png

# The project list is per machine: it holds absolute paths to folders on THIS disk, so
# committing it would hand every clone a list of directories that do not exist there.
projects.vngproj

# The clip list the animation window writes with SAVE. It is a working file about whatever
# spritesheet is in front of you, not something to ship: a clip is a rectangle on a canvas,
# and one committed here would be four numbers pointing at pixels nobody else has.
#
# vangopix_palette.ini is the opposite and IS committed - it holds the palettes of other
# machines, which are the same for everyone.
vangopix.anime
build/

# The key list the empty desk shows. Vangopix WRITES this one from its own defaults whenever
# it is not there, so committing it would be committing a copy that goes stale the moment the
# defaults change - and deleting it is the documented way to get those defaults back.
keyboard.txt

# The design document. It is the reasoning BEHIND this repository rather than part of it -
# a working notebook, kept beside the source and not shipped with it.
CLAUDE.md

# What `make dist` assembles on its way to the .zip. Derived from the tree beside it, and
# rebuilt from nothing every time - committing it would be committing a copy of the repo.
dist/
